> ### Recap of Adaptation and Its Importance
> 
> Adaptation to climate change refers to the process of adjusting to current or expected climatic variations and its effects. It is an integral part of tackling climate change, as it addresses the immediate and evolving challenges posed by a warming world. While mitigation efforts aim to reduce greenhouse gas emissions, adaptation focuses on minimizing the vulnerabilities and risks associated with climate impacts.
> 
> The reasons for investing in adaptation are multifaceted. Adaptation efforts are critical not only for protecting natural ecosystems, which serve as the lifeline for countless species, but also for safeguarding human health, infrastructure, and economic stability. These initiatives are invariably context-specific, due to the diverse array of local environmental, social, and economic conditions. Therefore, the design and implementation of adaptation measures must be tailored to the unique needs and capacities of each community.
> 
